.DS_Store

# GitHub refuses workflow files from an OAuth App token without the "workflow"
# scope. Measured 2026-11-16: `git push` of `.github/workflows/verify.yml` is
# rejected with
#   "refusing to allow an OAuth App to create or update workflow ... without
#    `workflow` scope"
# and the REST path is refused too — POST /git/trees carrying that path returns
# 404 (GitHub uses 404 rather than 403 for an insufficient-scope write).
#
# BOTH the gh CLI token and the Git Credential Manager credential lack the scope,
# so this cannot be fixed from inside a session: the OAuth device flow requires a
# human to approve the scope. To enable CI:
#   1. gh auth refresh -h github.com -s workflow   (approve the one-time code at
#                                                   https://github.com/login/device)
#      — or issue a fine-grained PAT with Workflows permission
#   2. delete this `.github/workflows/` line
#   3. git add -f .github/workflows/verify.yml && git commit && git push
# Until then there is NO CI: `.github/workflows/verify.yml` is a local-only file
# and the authoritative check is `npm run verify`.
.github/workflows/
